menu "Coprocessor board"

    config CP_RGB_LED_GPIO
        int "GPIO of the board's WS2812 RGB LED (-1 if none)"
        default -1
        range -1 48
        help
            Many dev boards have a WS2812 RGB LED that can come up lit after a
            reset. If set, the firmware sends it an "off" frame at boot and then
            holds the data line low.

endmenu
